Hello!

<br /><br />
<p>A link to this ShowMe.bxm file has been added
to the toc.bxm file by adding:</p>
        <code>
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#cgi.script_name#?p=ShowMe"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        </code>

<p>This passes in the variable <code>p</code></p>

<br /><br />
<p>In the learnBoxLang/index.bxm file, the line that references the toc.bxm file 
        uses the <code>include</code> component:</p>
        <code>
                &lt;bx:include template="toc.bxm"&gt;
        </code>
<br />
<p>In the learnBoxLang/index.bxm file, there is also a line that uses the <code>include</code> component 
        along with the value of the <code>p</code> variable inside a try-catch block, this would
        be the reference to this ShowMe.bxm file</p>

       <code> 
                &lt;bx:include template="#p#.bxm"&gt;
        </code>

<br /><br />
<p>This was the URL of this page when I was doing this assignment before I 
        set the name and port of the site using CommandBox:</p>
        <code>
                http://127.0.0.1:56343/index.bxm?p=ShowMe
        </code>

<p>This is the URL of this page after doing the Configuring Your Server step</p>
        <code>
                http://webclass.local/learnBoxLang/index.bxm?p=ShowMe
        </code>

<br /><br />
<p>The URL structure can be seen using <code>dump</code> and which shows the variable key/value pairs:</p>
        <code>
                &lt;bx:dump var="#url#" label="URL" /&gt;
        </code>

<br /><br />
<bx:dump var="#url#" label="URL" />


<br /><br />
<p>And the above <code>dump</code> display shows the addition of two more key/value pairs when the following 
        is appended to the end of the URL:</p>
        <code>
                &name=Bob&lastname=Marley
        </code>



